content.text:
You're absolutely right! The issue is that the client-side Marked.js code is processing all `.content` divs and converting any text content to markdown, which is interfering with the TodoWrite HTML structure.

Looking at lines 17-31, I can see the problem:

```javascript
// Find all content divs and render markdown
const contentDivs = document.querySelectorAll('.content');
contentDivs.forEach(div => {
    // Skip if it's already HTML (contains tags)
    if (div.innerHTML.includes('<pre>')) {
        return;
    }

    const markdownText = div.textContent;
    if (markdownText.trim()) {
        div.innerHTML = marked.parse(markdownText);
    }
});
```

The current logic only skips content that contains `<pre>` tags, but TodoWrite content has `<div>` tags instead. I need to update this to also skip content that contains TodoWrite HTML.

